724:<figure id="S3.F1" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="1905.00305v1/ONCF-gadget-small.svg" id="S3.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="width:30.642em; height:6.671em;aspect-ratio:407/89;" width="407" height="89"></object>
725:<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1: </span>The ONCF-gadget (left). Observe that if <math id="S3.F1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{1},g_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{1},g_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.F1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> are all red, then <math id="S3.F1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{9}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>9</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{9}</annotation></semantics></math> must also be red (middle), and if one of <math id="S3.F1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{1},g_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{1},g_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, or <math id="S3.F1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> is blue, then <math id="S3.F1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{9}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>9</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{9}</annotation></semantics></math> may be blue (right).</figcaption>
726-</figure>
727-<div id="S3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
728:<p id="S3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The objective of this gadget is the following. The vertices <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{g_{1},g_{2},g_{3},g_{10}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>10</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{g_{1},g_{2},g_{3},g_{10}\}</annotation></semantics></math> in Figure <a href="#S3.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 3.2 Running time lower bounds ‣ 3 Algorithmic results parameterized by treewidth ‣ Parameterized Complexity of Conflict-free Graph Coloring" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> will be the interaction points of the ONCF-gadget with the outside world. As will be proved in the following two lemmas, the gadget is designed so as to (i) disallow certain <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>-ONCF-colorings and (ii) allow certain <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>-ONCF-colorings on its interaction points.</p>
729-</div>
730-<div id="Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
731-<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span></h6>
732-<div id="Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para">
733:<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> be a ONCF-gadget with a coloring <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\colon V(G)\rightarrow\{\text{\emph{red}},\text{\emph{blue}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext><em class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">red</em></mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext><em class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">blue</em></mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\colon V(G)\rightarrow\{\text{\emph{red}},\text{\emph{blue}}\}</annotation></semantics></math> such that for all <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\leq i\leq 9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\leq i\leq 9</annotation></semantics></math> the neighborhood of <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is ONCF-colored by <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(g_{1})=c(g_{2})=c(g_{3})=\text{\emph{red}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mtext><em class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">red</em></mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(g_{1})=c(g_{2})=c(g_{3})=\text{\emph{red}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(g_{9})=\text{\emph{red}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>9</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mtext><em class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">red</em></mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(g_{9})=\text{\emph{red}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
734-</div>
