743-<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3</span></span></h6>
744-<div id="Thmlemma3.p1" class="ltx_para">
745:<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> be a ONCF-gadget. Let <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{\prime}\colon\{g_{1},g_{2},g_{3}\}\rightarrow\{\text{\emph{red}},\text{\emph{blue}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext><em class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">red</em></mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext><em class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">blue</em></mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{\prime}\colon\{g_{1},g_{2},g_{3}\}\rightarrow\{\text{\emph{red}},\text{\emph{blue}}\}</annotation></semantics></math> be a partial <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>-ONCF-coloring of <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>. If there exists <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[3]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[3]</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{\prime}(g_{i})=\text{\emph{blue}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mtext><em class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">blue</em></mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{\prime}(g_{i})=\text{\emph{blue}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> can be extended to a coloring <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying</span></p>
