775-<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproofx4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof</span></span></h6>
776-<div id="Thmproofx4.p1" class="ltx_para">
777:<p id="Thmproofx4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We show this by giving a reduction from <math id="Thmproofx4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>-<span id="Thmproofx4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">SAT</span>. Given an instance of <math id="Thmproofx4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>-<span id="Thmproofx4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">SAT</span> with variables <math id="Thmproofx4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},\ldots,x_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},\ldots,x_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and clauses <math id="Thmproofx4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1},\ldots,C_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1},\ldots,C_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, create a graph <math id="Thmproofx4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> as follows. Start by creating palette vertices <math id="Thmproofx4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R,R^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R,R^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmproofx4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, and edges <math id="Thmproofx4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{R,R^{\prime}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{R,R^{\prime}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmproofx4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{R^{\prime},B\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{R^{\prime},B\}</annotation></semantics></math>. For each variable <math id="Thmproofx4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>, create vertices <math id="Thmproofx4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i},v_{i},w_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i},v_{i},w_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and add edges <math id="Thmproofx4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{u_{i},v_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{u_{i},v_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmproofx4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{v_{i},w_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{v_{i},w_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. For the remainder of the construction we will reuse the ONCF-gadget as defined in Definition <a href="#Thmdefinition8" title="Definition 8 ‣ 3.2 Running time lower bounds ‣ 3 Algorithmic results parameterized by treewidth ‣ Parameterized Complexity of Conflict-free Graph Coloring" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>. For each <math id="Thmproofx4.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in[m]</annotation></semantics></math>, add an ONCF-gadget <math id="Thmproofx4.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> and connect <math id="Thmproofx4.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{10}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{10}</annotation></semantics></math> of this gadget to <math id="Thmproofx4.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>. Add vertices <math id="Thmproofx4.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{1}_{j},s^{2}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{1}_{j},s^{2}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmproofx4.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{3}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{3}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> and connect <math id="Thmproofx4.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{b}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{b}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="Thmproofx4.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{b}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="Thmproofx4.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Thmproofx4.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\in[3]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\in[3]</annotation></semantics></math>.
778-Let clause <math id="Thmproofx4.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{j}:=(\ell_{1},\ell_{2},\ell_{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{j}:=(\ell_{1},\ell_{2},\ell_{3})</annotation></semantics></math>. Now if <math id="Thmproofx4.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{b}=x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{b}=x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="Thmproofx4.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n],b\in[3]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n],b\in[3]</annotation></semantics></math>, connect <math id="Thmproofx4.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{b}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{b}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="Thmproofx4.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly, if <math id="Thmproofx4.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{b}=\neg x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">¬</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{b}=\neg x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, connect <math id="Thmproofx4.p1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{b}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{b}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="Thmproofx4.p1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. This concludes the construction of <math id="Thmproofx4.p1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>, it remains to show that <math id="Thmproofx4.p1.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="Thmproofx4.p1.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>-ONCF-colorable if and only if the formula was satisfiable.</p>
