784-<p id="Thmproofx4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> has a <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>-ONCF-coloring, we give a satisfying assignment <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>. Assume without loss of generality that <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(R):=\text{\emph{red}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><em class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">red</em></mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(R):=\text{\emph{red}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(v_{i}):=\{w_{i},u_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(v_{i}):=\{w_{i},u_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(u_{i})\neq c(w_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(u_{i})\neq c(w_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>. We therefore define <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau(x_{i}):=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau(x_{i}):=1</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(u_{i}):=\text{\emph{red}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><em class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">red</em></mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(u_{i}):=\text{\emph{red}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau(x_{i})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau(x_{i})=0</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(w_{i}):=\text{\emph{red}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><em class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">red</em></mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(w_{i}):=\text{\emph{red}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> be a clause, we will show that <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> to conclude the proof. Suppose for contradiction that <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> does not satisfy <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then every vertex <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{b}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{b}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\in[3]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\in[3]</annotation></semantics></math> had one neighbor in <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m19" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{u_{i},w_{i}\mid i\in[n]\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{u_{i},w_{i}\mid i\in[n]\}</annotation></semantics></math> that is <span id="Thmproofx4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath"><em id="Thmproofx4.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">blue</em></span> in <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>. Thereby, its only other neighbor <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{b}</annotation></semantics></math> in gadget <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> must be colored <span id="Thmproofx4.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath"><em id="Thmproofx4.p3.1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">red</em></span>. It follows from Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2 ‣ 3.2 Running time lower bounds ‣ 3 Algorithmic results parameterized by treewidth ‣ Parameterized Complexity of Conflict-free Graph Coloring" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> that <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(g_{9}):=\text{\emph{red}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>9</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><em class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">red</em></mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(g_{9}):=\text{\emph{red}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Observe however that <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(g_{10}):=\{g_{9},R\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>9</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(g_{10}):=\{g_{9},R\}</annotation></semantics></math> and that both these vertices are <span id="Thmproofx4.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath"><em id="Thmproofx4.p3.1.3.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">red</em></span>, contradicting that <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>-ONCF-coloring of <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, the formula is satisfied by <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
785-</div>
786-<div id="Thmproofx4.p4" class="ltx_para">
787:<p id="Thmproofx4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Note that the graph induced by <math id="Thmproofx4.p4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="V(G)\setminus\{u_{i},v_{i},w_{i}\mid i\in[n]\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(G)\setminus\{u_{i},v_{i},w_{i}\mid i\in[n]\}</annotation></semantics></math> is a disjoint union of ONCF-gadgets and has treewidth two. As such, <math id="Thmproofx4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> has treewidth at most <math id="Thmproofx4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3n+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3n+2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>

