923:<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2: </span>A sketch of the constructed graph <math id="S4.F2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S4.F2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=3</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.F2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=5</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.F2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=4</annotation></semantics></math>, assuming edge <math id="S4.F2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{5,4\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{5,4\}</annotation></semantics></math> is missing in instance <math id="S4.F2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and present in all other instances. All vertices created in Steps <a href="#S4.I1.i7" title="item 7 ‣ Proof ‣ 4.1 Kernel lower bounds for 𝑞-ONCF-Coloring ‣ 4 Kernelization ‣ Parameterized Complexity of Conflict-free Graph Coloring" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> and <a href="#S4.I1.i8" title="item 8 ‣ Proof ‣ 4.1 Kernel lower bounds for 𝑞-ONCF-Coloring ‣ 4 Kernelization ‣ Parameterized Complexity of Conflict-free Graph Coloring" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> of the construction are omitted for simplicity, except for vertex <math id="S4.F2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{1,2}_{5,4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{1,2}_{5,4}</annotation></semantics></math> and gadget <math id="S4.F2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{1,2}_{5,4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{1,2}_{5,4}</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
1024:<p id="Thmproofx15.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="Thmproofx15.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> be such that <math id="Thmproofx15.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> is a yes-instance for clique. Choose <math id="Thmproofx15.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j_{1},\ldots,j_{k}\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j_{1},\ldots,j_{k}\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math> such that these vertices form a clique in <math id="Thmproofx15.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>. We now give an ONCF-coloring <math id="Thmproofx15.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Thmproofx15.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>, see Figure <a href="#S4.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ Proof ‣ 4.1 Kernel lower bounds for 𝑞-ONCF-Coloring ‣ 4 Kernelization ‣ Parameterized Complexity of Conflict-free Graph Coloring" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> for an example ONCF-coloring of <math id="Thmproofx15.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
1187:For all remaining vertices, let <math id="Thmproofx19.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{\prime}(v):=q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{\prime}(v):=q</annotation></semantics></math>. It remains to show that this gives a <math id="Thmproofx19.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>-ONCF-coloring of <math id="Thmproofx19.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. See Figure <a href="#S4.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ Proof ‣ Proof ‣ 4.1 Kernel lower bounds for 𝑞-ONCF-Coloring ‣ 4 Kernelization ‣ Parameterized Complexity of Conflict-free Graph Coloring" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> for a sketch of <math id="Thmproofx19.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
1189:<figure id="S4.F3" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="1905.00305v1/ONCF-poly-param-transformation.svg" id="S4.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="width:34.609em; height:9.155em;aspect-ratio:460/122;" width="460" height="122"></object>
1190:<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span>Reduction from <math id="S4.F3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.F3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S4.F3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=5</annotation></semantics></math>. The subdivided edges from <math id="S4.F3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.F3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> added in Step <a href="#S4.I4.i4" title="item 4 ‣ Proof ‣ 4.1 Kernel lower bounds for 𝑞-ONCF-Coloring ‣ 4 Kernelization ‣ Parameterized Complexity of Conflict-free Graph Coloring" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> of the construction are omitted for simplicity.</figcaption>
1231:<p id="S4.I6.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I6.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of a single isolated vertex. <math id="S4.I6.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S4.I6.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{1,3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{1,3}</annotation></semantics></math> with one edge subdivided by another vertex (refer also to Figure <a href="#S4.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 4.2 Kernel lower bound for CNCF-Coloring ‣ 4 Kernelization ‣ Parameterized Complexity of Conflict-free Graph Coloring" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>).</p>
1270:<p id="Thmdefinition10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To create a <em id="Thmdefinition10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">palette-gadget</em> <math id="Thmdefinition10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> start from a complete graph on vertices <math id="Thmdefinition10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1},\ldots,c_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1},\ldots,c_{q}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, add vertices <math id="Thmdefinition10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Thmdefinition10.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[q]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[q]</annotation></semantics></math> and connect <math id="Thmdefinition10.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="Thmdefinition10.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmdefinition10.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="Thmdefinition10.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D:=\{c_{i},c_{i}^{\prime}\mid i\in[q]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D:=\{c_{i},c_{i}^{\prime}\mid i\in[q]</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of distinguished vertices of the gadget. Finally, for each edge <math id="Thmdefinition10.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{u,v\}\in E(C_{q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{u,v\}\in E(C_{q})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmdefinition10.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u,v\in D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u,v\in D</annotation></semantics></math>, add two new distinct copies of <math id="Thmdefinition10.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{q-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{q-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and connect all vertices in these copies to both <math id="Thmdefinition10.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmdefinition10.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>. See Figure <a href="#S4.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 4.2 Kernel lower bound for CNCF-Coloring ‣ 4 Kernelization ‣ Parameterized Complexity of Conflict-free Graph Coloring" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> for an example of the palette-gadget <math id="Thmdefinition10.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
1273:<figure id="S4.F4" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="1905.00305v1/cncf-palette-2.svg" id="S4.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="width:26.630em; height:8.381em;aspect-ratio:354/111;" width="354" height="111"></object>
1338:<figure id="S4.F5" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="1905.00305v1/cross-composition-CNCF.svg" id="S4.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="width:34.142em; height:13.529em;aspect-ratio:454/180;" width="454" height="180"></object>
1339:<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span>A sketch of the constructed graph <math id="S4.F5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S4.F5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=3</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.F5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=3</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.F5.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=5</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.F5.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=4</annotation></semantics></math>. All vertices created in Steps <a href="#S4.I8.i7" title="item 7 ‣ Proof ‣ 4.2 Kernel lower bound for CNCF-Coloring ‣ 4 Kernelization ‣ Parameterized Complexity of Conflict-free Graph Coloring" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> and <a href="#S4.I8.i8" title="item 8 ‣ Proof ‣ 4.2 Kernel lower bound for CNCF-Coloring ‣ 4 Kernelization ‣ Parameterized Complexity of Conflict-free Graph Coloring" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> are omitted, except those created with <math id="S4.F5.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.F5.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i^{\prime}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i^{\prime}=2</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.F5.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=5</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.F5.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j^{\prime}=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j^{\prime}=4</annotation></semantics></math>, assuming edge <math id="S4.F5.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{4,5\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{4,5\}</annotation></semantics></math> is not present in instance <math id="S4.F5.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. The palette <math id="S4.F5.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is omitted, edges to the palette are drawn as arrows.</figcaption>
1342:<p id="Thmproofx22.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We define the same polynomial equivalence relation; let two instances of <span id="Thmproofx22.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Clique</span> be equivalent if the graphs have the same number of vertices and they ask for a clique of the same size. Suppose we are given <math id="Thmproofx22.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> instances of clique that are equivalent under this relation, labeled <math id="Thmproofx22.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1},\ldots,X_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1},\ldots,X_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let every instance have <math id="Thmproofx22.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> vertices and ask for a clique of size <math id="Thmproofx22.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>. We enumerate the vertices in each instance arbitrarily as <math id="Thmproofx22.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1,\ldots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1,\ldots,n</annotation></semantics></math>. We create an instance <math id="Thmproofx22.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Thmproofx22.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>-<span id="Thmproofx22.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">CNCF-Coloring</span> by the following steps, refer to Figure <a href="#S4.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ Proof ‣ 4.2 Kernel lower bound for CNCF-Coloring ‣ 4 Kernelization ‣ Parameterized Complexity of Conflict-free Graph Coloring" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> for a sketch of <math id="Thmproofx22.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
1431:<p id="Thmproofx25.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Take <math id="Thmproofx25.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Thmproofx25.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> is a yes-instance for <span id="Thmproofx25.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Clique</span> and let <math id="Thmproofx25.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j_{1},\ldots,j_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j_{1},\ldots,j_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> be such that vertices <math id="Thmproofx25.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{j_{1},\ldots,j_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{j_{1},\ldots,j_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> form this clique in instance <math id="Thmproofx25.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>. We give a coloring <math id="Thmproofx25.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c:V(G)\rightarrow[q]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c:V(G)\rightarrow[q]</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="Thmproofx25.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>. We start by showing how to color the vertices defined in each step of the construction, this coloring is also depicted in Figure <a href="#S4.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ Proof ‣ 4.2 Kernel lower bound for CNCF-Coloring ‣ 4 Kernelization ‣ Parameterized Complexity of Conflict-free Graph Coloring" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</p>
1814:<p id="Thmproofx34.p3.1" class="ltx_p">It is known that the <span id="Thmproofx34.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Monotone Exact Sat</span> problem is NP-hard, as it generalizes problem <span id="Thmproofx34.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">NP1</span> in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>]</cite>. Let an instance <math id="Thmproofx34.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}=C_{1}\wedge\dots\wedge C_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∧</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}=C_{1}\wedge\dots\wedge C_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> over variables <math id="Thmproofx34.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=\{x_{1},\ldots,x_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=\{x_{1},\ldots,x_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math> be given, we show how to construct a graph <math id="Thmproofx34.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> with vertex cover <math id="Thmproofx34.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> and precoloring <math id="Thmproofx34.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\colon S\rightarrow\{\text{\emph{red}},\text{\emph{blue}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><em class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">red</em></mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><em class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">blue</em></mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\colon S\rightarrow\{\text{\emph{red}},\text{\emph{blue}}\}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Thmproofx34.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>-<span id="Thmproofx34.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">CNCF-Coloring-VC-Extension</span>. See Figure <a href="#S4.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ Proof ‣ 4.4 Kernelization bounds for conflict-free coloring extension ‣ 4 Kernelization ‣ Parameterized Complexity of Conflict-free Graph Coloring" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> for a sketch of <math id="Thmproofx34.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
